---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---

<DocsLayout title="Passkey">
  <h1>Passkey (WebAuthn)</h1>
  <p>
    Passkeys are a phishing-resistant first factor backed by
    <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/">WebAuthn</a>. Identity
    handles the server side of the ceremony with
    <code>github.com/go-webauthn/webauthn</code>. The browser does the
    actual public-key crypto via
    <code>navigator.credentials.create()</code> and
    <code>navigator.credentials.get()</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Configuration</h2>
  <p>
    The relying-party (RP) identifiers must match the domain users will
    sign in from, or browsers will refuse the ceremony.
  </p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Variable</th><th>Example</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GATEWAY_PASSKEY_RP_ID</code></td><td><code>example.com</code> — registrable domain, no scheme, no port</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GATEWAY_PASSKEY_RP_NAME</code></td><td><code>Example</code> — shown in the OS dialog</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GATEWAY_PASSKEY_ORIGIN</code></td><td><code>https://app.example.com</code> — full origin including scheme</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Registration</h2>
  <p>
    The user must already be authenticated (e.g. they signed in with
    password). The flow is two RPCs.
  </p>

  <h3>1. Begin</h3>
  <Code code={`curl -sX POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/BeginPasskeyRegistration \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"deviceName":"Alice's MacBook"}'`} lang="bash" />
  <Code code={`{
  "optionsJson": "{\\"challenge\\":...,\\"rp\\":{\\"id\\":\\"example.com\\",...}}",
  "challengeId": "ch_..."
}`} lang="json" />
  <p>
    The browser passes <code>options_json</code> straight to
    <code>navigator.credentials.create()</code> after JSON-parsing.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Complete</h3>
  <Code code={`const options = JSON.parse(beginResponse.options_json);
const credential = await navigator.credentials.create(options);

await fetch("/identity.IdentityService/CompletePasskeyRegistration", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Authorization": "Bearer " + token, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    challengeId: beginResponse.challenge_id,
    credentialJson: JSON.stringify(credential),
    deviceName: "Alice's MacBook",
  }),
});`} lang="javascript" />

  <h2>Login</h2>
  <p>
    No prior session is needed.
    <code>BeginPasskeyLogin</code> with an empty <code>email</code>
    permits discoverable credentials (the browser shows whichever passkey
    the user picks); supplying an email scopes the ceremony to that
    user's keys.
  </p>
  <Code code={`// 1. Ask Identity for options
const begin = await fetch("/identity.IdentityService/BeginPasskeyLogin", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ email: "" }),  // discoverable credentials
}).then(r => r.json());

// 2. Browser does the ceremony
const credential = await navigator.credentials.get(JSON.parse(begin.options_json));

// 3. Hand the assertion back to Identity
const complete = await fetch("/identity.IdentityService/CompletePasskeyLogin", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    challengeId: begin.challenge_id,
    credentialJson: JSON.stringify(credential),
  }),
}).then(r => r.json());

// complete.access_token, complete.refresh_token, complete.user`} lang="javascript" />

  <h2>Managing passkeys</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>ListPasskeys</code> — returns the credentials registered to the calling user, with <code>created_at</code> and <code>last_used_at</code>.</li>
    <li><code>DeletePasskey</code> — removes a credential by ID. Audit-logged.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Storage</h2>
  <p>
    Passkey credentials are relational rows in the datastore, linked to
    their owning <code>User</code>. The stored fields are the
    credential ID, the public key, the sign counter, and the user's
    chosen device label — never any private material.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
